# Lean language policy

- Read AGENTS.md and docs/plans/project-language-policy.md.
- Spanish public UI includes errors, accessibility, help/privacy, insights and exports; code/keys/routes/schema/comments/tests/docs are English.
- Use lang/es semantic catalogs and es default/fallback. Keep existing key/placeholder/browser checks; no raw errors or missing keys.
- ca/gl/eu are optional later complete public packs, not core blockers. No mandatory human/fluent certification or quorum. Disable incomplete/uncertain packs.
- Original source quotations/names remain exact; label translated paraphrases separately with access to the original.
- Locale changes preserve semantic question/answer IDs, scales, weights, scores and citations. Private state stays local.
- No admin language work, reviewer roster or expanded language-governance platform.
